      "side": 1,
      "message": "As discussed in https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jB8bFmveVX3KCHhJvwojkFkCcrNZgIId5menRfIuvJU/edit?resourcekey\u003d0-liWSXra6n1pGy8Cz4gri1Q#, we will run the ATT TS using pts-bot on the Java API.\n\nRegarding non-transactional operations, they are planned for this implementation, and will be added in a future CL (roughly speaking, the `AttServerBearer#handle_packet` implementation will switch on the command bit to decide whether to use the `AttTransactionHandler` or a separate to-be-written `AttCommandHandler` that does not enforce the transactional semantics).\n\nRegarding timers, I don\u0027t see how client transaction timeouts belong here - since the server will never timeout during normal operation. Timeouts exist in the CallbackTransactionManager and will be added to support indications, but are not (IMO) necessary elsewhere.",
